package com.github.piotr.rusin.yule;
Reason: The test class `YuleApplicationTests.java` was declared under the package `com.github.piotr.rusin.yule` (using a dot between "piotr" and "rusin"), which does not match the actual package of the main application class. Since Spring Boot's test context initialization searches for a `@SpringBootApplication` class starting from the test's own package and moving upward, this mismatched package caused the search to fail, resulting in "No application configuration could be found."

The code statements that fix the bug are:
package com.github.piotr_rusin.yule;
Reason: By renaming the package declaration in the test class to `com.github.piotr_rusin.yule` (using an underscore, matching the main application's package structure), the test class now resides in the correct package hierarchy. This allows Spring Boot's component scanning to correctly locate the `@SpringBootApplication`-annotated main class, enabling proper test context initialization.

